From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(fusion): record why neither fusion tree can replace the
 other

Both trees now do turbo3/turbo4 KV correctly, so that is no longer the separator.
Two things are:

- The private type sets are disjoint. TQ3_1S/TQ4_1S (45/46) exist only on the b11046
  branch; PQ2_0/PTQ1_0 (142/143) exist only here. Measured, not inferred:
  llama-cli -m Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0.gguf on b11046 -> rc=1 in 1 s with
  "tensor 'output.weight' has invalid ggml type 142. should be in [0, 47)".
- Turbo KV is at parity: SC117 head_dim 256, f16 6.9921 vs 6.9422, turbo3 7.1292 vs
  7.1626, turbo4 7.0756 vs 7.0895. Neither tree is better at it.

Also records the deployment split read out of the launchers (Bonsai -> this tree's
build-hip; SC117 and ISTA -> the promoted b10335 runtime), so the two trees are not
two copies of one thing, and the direction of any future consolidation: port
PrismQL's private types forward onto b11046, never move b11046 back 430 commits
(35 of them in ggml-cuda, 75 in src/, including FA correctness fixes).
