+---
+
+## Can this tree replace llama.cpp-turboquant-fusion? No - measured (2026-09-19)
+
+Both trees now do turbo3/turbo4 KV correctly, so the capability that used to be the
+headline is no longer what separates them. Two things do, and both are hard blocks
+rather than matters of degree.
+
+### 1. The private type sets are disjoint
+
+| type | this tree (PrismML base) | llama.cpp-turboquant fusion (b11046) |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| TURBO3_0 = 43 (KV cache) | yes | yes |
+| TURBO4_0 = 44 (KV cache) | yes | yes |
+| TQ3_1S = 45 (weight, block 32) | **no** | yes |
+| TQ4_1S = 46 (weight, block 32) | **no** | yes |
+| PQ2_0 = 142 (ternary weight, group 128) | yes | **no** |
+| PTQ1_0 = 143 (ternary weight, group 128) | yes | **no** |
+
+Neither tree is a superset. `ggml.h` on the b11046 branch stops at `GGML_TYPE_COUNT =
+47`, so the target model cannot even be opened there:
+
+```text
+$ llama-cli -m Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0.gguf -p hi -n 1 -c 256
+gguf_init_from_reader: tensor 'output.weight' has invalid ggml type 142. should be in [0, 47)
+rc=1 in 1 s
+```
+
+Record: `bench-results/tree-equivalence/b11046-load-bonsai.log`.
+
+### 2. Turbo KV is at parity, so neither tree wins on it
+
+SC117, head_dim 256, `-c 512 -fa 1 --chunks 8 -ngl 999`:
+
+| KV | this tree | b11046 tree |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| f16 x f16 | 6.9921 | 6.9422 |
+| turbo3 x turbo3 | 7.1292 | 7.1626 |
+| turbo4 x turbo4 | 7.0756 | 7.0895 |
+
+Same-GPU, same model, same settings. Both are healthy; the deltas against their own
+f16 are +2.0% and +3.2% for turbo3, which is the same order as the cross-build
+difference on f16 alone.
+
+### They already occupy different slots
+
+Read out of the launchers, so this is what runs rather than what could run:
+
+| model | entry point | binary |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B | `start-bonsai.bat` | `sources/PrismML-turboquant-fusion/build-hip/bin` |
+| SC117 (fast / 200k) | `start-fast.bat`, `start-200k.bat` | `runtimes/llama.cpp-turboquant-fusion-rocm71-gfx1030-b10335` |
+| ISTA Qwen3.8-27B (256k) | `start-256k.bat` | same promoted runtime |
+
+So this is not two copies of one thing: one is the ternary model's build, the other is
+the promoted serving runtime for everything else.
+
+### If consolidation is ever wanted, the direction is forward
+
+Port the PrismML-private types (PQ2_0 142 / PTQ1_0 143: block layout, CPU codec,
+MMQ/MMVQ/MMF kernels, dequantise, convert tables) **onto the b11046 base**, so Bonsai
+also rides the newer upstream. Going the other way - moving b11046 back to this tree's
+merge-base (`b10615-1`) - would drop 430 upstream commits, 35 of them in
+`ggml/src/ggml-cuda` and 75 in `src/`, including FA correctness work such as
+`b74f590ea fix divergent barrier in f16 flash attention` and the
+`ad6c66839` BF16-acceleration fallback that a gfx1030 host needs. That direction is
+pure regression and should not be on the table.
+
+The cost of that forward port is real, but it is the same shape as the one already done
+twice, and `scripts/audit-port-deletions.py` now exists to prove nothing is silently
+dropped along the way.
+
+
